p.src:
An observer can count standard sources in a redshift bin $z$ to $z+dz$. Begin with equation  and differentiate equation  along the past light ray: $dz=-\frac{a_0}{a^2}\,da
=-\frac{a_0}{a^2}\dot a\,dt.$ Using $dt=-a\,dr$, $dz=\frac{a_0}{a}\dot a\,dr
=(1+z)\dot a\,dr.$ Hence $dr=\frac{dz}{(1+z)\dot a},$ and, for a fixed comoving source density, $\boxed{
\frac{dN}{dz}
\propto
\frac{\xi(r)^2}{(1+z)\dot a}
}.$ The live derivation checks signs and factors more than once; equations  and  fix the result unambiguously.

